{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":98186,"duration_api_ms":94560,"ttft_ms":8215,"ttft_stream_ms":7123,"time_to_request_ms":173,"num_turns":21,"result":"Confirmed the intended behavior: repeated calls with identical args within a run hit the cache (no re-run of `df`), different args get their own cache entries, and clearing `__context__` (which Salt does between independent runs/jobs) forces a fresh lookup.\n\n## Summary\n\nModified `usage()` in `salt/modules/disk.py:79` to cache its result in `__context__`, keyed by the cleaned flag string (`disk.usage.<flags>`). This is Salt's standard per-run cache dict — it persists across execution-module calls within a single job/state run but is destroyed and recreated for each new run, so:\n\n- Repeated `disk.usage()` calls with the same args in one run skip `df` entirely.\n- Different `args` get independent cache entries.\n- Separate, independent Salt runs never see stale data, since `__context__` doesn't survive between them.\n\nThe function signature and return format are unchanged. Existing unit tests in `tests/pytests/unit/modules/test_disk.py` pass (25 passed, 6 skipped for unrelated platform reasons).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"1cbcf6a3-c85c-4ae2-b1e9-81233ffdbb6d","total_cost_usd":0.6709985999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":50369,"cache_read_input_tokens":958622,"output_tokens":5405,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":50369,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":41,"outputTokens":5405,"cacheReadInputTokens":958622,"cacheCreationInputTokens":50369,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6709985999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_st